[ti:Smash-and-Grab]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.42]Lesson 6 | 第6课
[00:02.22]Smash-and-grab | 砸橱窗抢劫
[00:08.70]How did Mr. Taylor try to stop the thieves? | 泰勒先生是怎样试图拦住窃贼的？
[00:13.91]The expensive shops in a famous arcade near Piccadilly were just opening. | 皮卡迪利大街附近一条著名拱廊街道上的高档商店刚刚开门。
[00:19.86]At this time of the morning, the arcade was almost empty. | 早晨的这个时刻，拱廊街上几乎空无一人。
[00:24.53]Mr. Taylor, the owner of a jewellery shop was admiring a new window display. | 珠宝店老板泰勒先生正在欣赏新布置的橱窗。
[00:30.92]Two of his assistants had been working busily since 8 o'clock and had only just finished. | 两名店员从早上8点就一直忙着布置，刚刚才完工。
[00:38.10]Diamond necklaces and rings had been beautifully arranged on a background of black velvet. | 钻石项链和戒指漂亮地陈列在黑丝绒衬底上。
[00:45.36]After gazing at the display for several minutes, Mr. Taylor went back into his shop. | 泰勒先生注视着橱窗几分钟之后，便回到了店里。
[00:52.13]The silence was suddenly broken when a large car, with its headlights on and its horn blaring, roared down the arcade. | 宁静突然被打破，一辆大桥车亮着前灯、鸣着喇叭，呼啸着冲下拱廊街。
[01:01.86]It came to a stop outside the jeweller's. | 它在珠宝店门外停了下来。
[01:05.68]One man stayed at the wheel while two others with black stockings over their faces jumped out and smashed the window of the shop with iron bars. | 一人留在驾驶座上，另外两个脸上蒙着黑色针织面罩的人跳下车，用铁棒砸碎了商店的橱窗。
[01:16.82]While this was going on, Mr. Taylor was upstairs. | 这一切发生时，泰勒先生正在楼上。
[01:21.36]He and his staff began throwing furniture out of the window. | 他和店员动手往窗外扔家具。
[01:26.25]Chairs and tables went flying into the arcade. | 椅子和桌子飞落到拱廊街上。
[01:30.59]One of the thieves was struck by a heavy statue, | 一名窃贼被一尊很重的雕像击中，
[01:34.21]but he was too busy helping himself to diamonds to notice any pain. | 但他只顾忙着抓钻石，顾不上疼痛了。
[01:40.36]The raid was all over in three minutes, for the men scrambled back into the car and it moved off at a fantastic speed. | 这场抢劫只持续了3分钟，因为窃贼争先恐后地爬回轿车，然后以惊人的速度开走了。
[01:50.19]Just as it was leaving, | 就在轿车离开的时候，
[01:52.38]Mr.Taylor rushed out and ran after it throwing ashtrays and vases, | 泰勒先生冲了出来，跟在车后追，边追边扔烟灰缸和花瓶，
[01:57.86]but it was impossible to stop the thieves. | 但已不可能拦住窃贼了。
[02:00.99]They had got away with thousands of pounds worth of diamonds. | 他们带着价值数千英镑的钻石逃之夭夭。
